2. NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS

2.1 Outgoing business email

Resend is the sole provider for outgoing business email.

All business-email sending must follow:

"Frontend or internal workflow → Rentmaikar Cloud Run backend → Resend API → Recipient"

The frontend must never send business email directly through Resend.

All business-email operations must be mediated by the backend, which must authenticate and authorise the initiating user or internal workflow, validate the message, enforce applicable tenant and role restrictions, and record the outcome.

Do not implement automatic provider failover.

Do not silently substitute SendGrid, SMTP, Gmail, Nodemailer with external SMTP, Twilio, Termii, or any other provider if Resend is unavailable.

If Resend fails, return or record a controlled failure, apply safe retry rules where appropriate, and expose the actual outcome through monitoring.

Nodemailer or another library may be used only if it is genuinely necessary for a permitted implementation and does not introduce an alternative delivery provider. Prefer the official Resend SDK or supported Resend API.

