Do not store full sensitive message bodies unless necessary and explicitly governed by retention controls.

Use a transactional outbox or equivalent durable queue if the existing system requires reliable asynchronous sending.

Enforce uniqueness constraints or equivalent atomic controls on idempotency keys.

Do not retry permanent failures indefinitely. Use bounded retries with exponential backoff and jitter for transient failures, respecting provider guidance.

Do not resend a message merely because a status webhook was delayed.

Ensure the system distinguishes an API request being accepted from actual delivery.

